@startuml
title Shelter Map - Shelter API (read + write)
' Thin controllers (Ch 1: service providers for HTTP) - parse, validate, delegate, map. No business logic.
' DTO records are the versioned contract with the frontend (Vue/Angular).
' Machine-readable companion: docs/api/openapi.json (committed snapshot,
' regenerated by OpenApiSnapshotIT) + the dev-only /swagger-ui (springdoc,
' opt-in via SPRINGDOC_ENABLED).
' Depends only on interfaces from other contexts (01): ShelterRepository, ShelterService, UserRepository.

package "api" {
  class ShelterController {
    + GET    /api/shelters?source=REGISTRY|USER|ALL  ' + optional trust filters (V9)
    + GET    /api/shelters/{id}
    + POST   /api/shelters
    + GET    /api/shelters/mine
    + PUT    /api/shelters/{id}
    + DELETE /api/shelters/{id}
    + POST   /api/shelters/{id}/reports      ' 200 {"damped": bool}; 403/404/409/429
    + PUT    /api/shelters/{id}/occupancy    ' V9: 204 upsert; 404/429
  }

  class LocationController {
    ' shelter-location-input (8686b99) - thin shell for the short-link
    ' resolver: parse, validate, delegate, map (Ch 1). JWT-protected
    ' (inside the authenticated set, NOT permitAll) + per-IP 5/min
    ' token bucket (geoResolveRateLimiter, keys via ClientIps - auth/03).
    + POST /api/geo/resolve (body : LocationResolveRequest) : LocationResolvedDto
  }

  class AdminController {
    ' admin-moderation D3 - the /admin/* moderation surface. Thin shell:
    ' parse, validate, AUTHORIZE, delegate. Authorization (D2): a FRESH
    ' UserRepository.isAdmin(userId) kind lookup PER REQUEST - never a JWT
    ' claim (a demotion takes effect on the very next request). 401
    ' anonymous (the security entry point - /admin/** is in the
    ' authenticated set), 403 authenticated non-admin (AdminAccessException).
    + GET    /admin/shelters?status=&source=&q=   : List<AdminShelterDto>   ' ALL statuses incl. hidden
    + POST   /admin/shelters/{id}/status (body : AdminShelterStatusRequest) : 204  ' USER rows only; restore disarms auto-hide
    + DELETE /admin/shelters/{id} : 204                     ' hard delete (cascade); USER rows only
    + GET    /admin/reports?shelterId= : List<AdminShelterReportDto>  ' shelter-report queue, newest first
    + POST   /admin/reports/{id}/dismiss : 204              ' idempotent; the row is KEPT
    + POST   /admin/shelters/{id}/review (body : AdminShelterReviewRequest) : 200 {"ok": true}  ' V11: CONFIRM/REJECT (reason required for REJECT); USER rows only
    + GET    /admin/audit?limit= : List<AdminAuditDto>      ' V11: newest-first moderation trail; limit 1..200 (default 100)
    + GET    /admin/alerts?limit= : List<AdminAlertDto>     ' M3 s4: in-memory throttle/abuse alert ring; limit 1..200 (default 50)
    + GET    /admin/shelters/{id}/history : List<AdminShelterHistoryDto>  ' M10 s2: CREATED/EDITED/DELETED trail (server-parsed diffs); 404 only absent + no history
    + POST   /admin/shelters/{id}/request-info (body : AdminInfoRequestRequest) : 204  ' M10 s3: moderator -> submitter info request; one exchange per shelter; reply via POST /api/shelters/{id}/info-request/reply
    + POST   /admin/shelters/{id}/mark-inaccurate (body : AdminMarkInaccurateRequest) : 204  ' M10 s4: public inaccurate flag (row STAYS visible); idempotent; audited
    + POST   /admin/shelters/{id}/clear-inaccurate : 204   ' M10 s4: clears the flag; idempotent; audited
    + GET    /admin/users : List<AdminUserDto>             ' M10 s1: REGISTERED + ADMIN accounts (id, name, email, kind, suspendedAt); GUEST absent
    + POST   /admin/users/{id}/suspend : 204               ' M10 s1: REGISTERED only (409 else); idempotent; audited, account as subject; enforced at login/refresh/JWT doors
    + POST   /admin/users/{id}/unsuspend : 204             ' M10 s1: clears suspended_at; idempotent; audited
  }

  class AdminModerationService {
    ' admin-moderation D3/D4 - owns the guard rails (the controller
    ' authorizes; this service guards). All writes are single-row
    ' transactions; no bulk endpoints; every unknown id -> 404.
    + listShelters(status : ShelterStatus, source : ShelterSource, q : String) : List<AdminShelterDto>
    + setShelterStatus(shelterId : long, target : ShelterStatus) : void
    ' USER rows only (source != USER -> 409 ImportOwnedShelterException - D4).
    ' A restore (INACTIVE -> ACTIVE) sets autoHideDisarmed = true - the
    ' manual-change marker that PERMANENTLY disarms auto-hide (V9 D1).
    + deleteShelter(shelterId : long) : void
    ' USER rows only (409); the DB cascades shelter reports, occupancy and
    ' open-status rows (all FKs ON DELETE CASCADE).
    + listShelterReports(shelterId : Long) : List<AdminShelterReportDto>
    ' newest first (created_at desc, id desc tie-break); optional shelterId
    ' (unknown shelter -> 404); shelter status + reporter name/email in ONE
    ' batched lookup each (no N+1).
    + dismissReport(reportId : long) : void
    ' stamps dismissed_at ONCE (idempotent - a re-dismiss is a no-op);
    ' the row is KEPT (records the resolution, never deletes).
    ' ---- V11 (community-review-queue v2) ----
    + reviewShelter(moderatorId : long, shelterId : long, action : ReviewDecision, reason : String) : void
    ' USER rows only (registry -> 409); CONFIRM: review_status = CONFIRMED, note cleared,
    ' status untouched (it does NOT un-hide); REJECT: reason REQUIRED (else 400),
    ' review_status = REJECTED AND status = INACTIVE (the existing hide mechanism).
    ' Both write their audit row (CONFIRM / REJECT) in the SAME transaction.
    + listAudit(moderatorId : long, limit : int) : List<AdminAuditDto>
    ' newest-first moderation_actions (default 100, 1..200); read-time shelter/moderator
    ' name resolution - a deleted shelter renders "Deleted shelter" (shelter_id has no FK).
  }

  class AdminShelterStatusRequest <<record>> {
    + status : ShelterStatus   ' @NotNull - {"status": "ACTIVE" | "INACTIVE"};
                               ' missing/unknown -> 400 (standard vocabulary)
  }

  class AdminShelterReviewRequest <<record>> {
    ' V11 (community-review-queue v2): the rare manual review decision.
    + action : ReviewDecision    ' @NotNull - {"action": "CONFIRM" | "REJECT"}
    + reason : String            ' @Size(max = 500) - REQUIRED for REJECT (blank -> 400);
    ' optional for CONFIRM; stored on the shelter as review_note (shown in /mine)
  }

  class AdminAuditDto <<record>> {
    ' V11 (community-review-queue v2): one row of GET /admin/audit (newest first,
    ' newest 100 by default, limit 1..200).
    + id : Long
    + shelterId : Long           ' deliberately FK-free in the DB - dangling after a delete
    + shelterName : String       ' read-time join; "Deleted shelter" when the row is gone
    + moderatorName : String     ' read-time name resolution; "Deleted user" when gone
    + action : String            ' STATUS_CHANGE | DELETE | REPORT_DISMISS | CONFIRM |
    '                             ' AUTO_CONFIRM | REJECT
    + reason : String            ' the REJECT note, when set
    + previousStatus : ReviewStatus  ' the review_status around the action
    + newStatus : ReviewStatus       ' (DELETE: previous = the row's state, new = null)
    + createdAt : Instant
  }

  class AdminShelterDto <<record>> {
    ' One row of GET /admin/shelters - every shelter, ALL statuses
    ' (auto-hidden rows included), id-ordered: the public projection's
    ' trust fields plus what the public list hides.
    + id : Long
    + name : String
    + address : String
    + source : ShelterSource
    + status : ShelterStatus       ' incl. INACTIVE (auto-hidden)
    + nonexistentReports : int     ' 0 when none
    + occupancy : Occupancy        ' the fresh (<= 2 h) block; null when nothing fresh
    + capacity : Integer
    + submitter : String           ' the creator's profile name; null for registry
                                   ' rows and for deleted creators
    + reviewStatus : ReviewStatus  ' V11 (community-review-queue v2): NEW / CONFIRMED /
                                   ' REJECTED; the Unconfirmed tab = USER + NEW rows
    + reviewNote : String          ' V11: the REJECT reason; null while nothing is said
    + locationKind : LocationKind  ' V11: the private-home declaration (badge only)
    + provenance : Provenance      ' V12 (shelter-provenance-taxonomy): the
                                   ' server-derived source answer (never re-derived)
    + inaccurate : boolean         ' M10 slice 4 (V20 stamp): the moderator's
                                   ' "inaccurate" flag; the row stays visible
    + infoRequest : InfoRequest    ' M10 slice 3: the moderator-to-submitter
                                   ' exchange (message, requestedAt, replyMessage,
                                   ' repliedAt)
  }

  class AdminShelterReportDto <<record>> {
    ' One row of the shelter-report queue. Reporter identity is ADMIN-ONLY
    ' data - never exposed outside /admin/*.
    + id : Long
    + shelterId : Long
    + shelterName : String
    + shelterStatus : ShelterStatus  ' the shelter's LIVE status (drives the UI restore shortcut)
    + type : ShelterReportType
    + detail : String
    + reporterName : String
    + reporterEmail : String
    + createdAt : Instant
    + dismissed : boolean          ' dismissed_at != null; dismissed rows stay in the queue
  }

  class LocationResolveRequest <<record>> {
    + url : String   ' @NotBlank @Size(max = 2048)
  }

  class LocationResolvedDto <<record>> {
    + latitude : double
    + longitude : double
    ' Field names are the frontend contract (LocationResolved) - do not rename.
  }

  class ShelterQueryService {
    + findAll(source : ShelterSourceFilter, hasCapacity : Boolean, provenance : Provenance) : List<ShelterDto>
    + findById(id : Long, caller : User) : Optional<ShelterDto>
    + findByCreatedBy(userId : Long) : List<ShelterDto>
    ' M8 author-scoped list - same lean DTO projection (no N+1).
    ' V9 (D5): the public list is ACTIVE rows only (auto-hidden shelters are
    ' absent); the trust filter (hasCapacity) is applied
    ' in-memory over the projection - no new SQL surface. (M11: the rating
    ' filter is gone - a stray param is ignored, not an error.)
    ' findById is
    ' the detail read (ALL statuses; the single-shelter read carries
    ' yourOccupancyBand). The trust derivations (nonexistentReports, the
    ' fresh open/closed + occupancy blocks) ride the same batched pass.
  }

  class ShelterDto <<record>> {
    + id : Long
    + name : String
    + address : String
    + latitude : double
    + longitude : double
    + status : ShelterStatus
    + source : ShelterSource
    + createdAt : Instant
    + description : String
    + capacity : Integer
    + submitterVerified : boolean  ' accessibility-and-provenance D3: creator
                                   ' exists + verification COMPLETED; false for
                                   ' registry rows (no author) and for deleted
                                   ' creators (absent from the findByIds batch)
    + nonexistentReports : int     ' V9 (D1): 0 when none; > 0 = the orange
                                   ' "Reported" affordance (derived, not stored)
    + openStatus : OpenStatus      ' V22 (open-status): the fresh (<= 2 h)
                                   ' open/closed block; null when nothing fresh
    + occupancy : Occupancy        ' V9 (D4): the fresh (<= 2 h) block; null
                                   ' when nothing fresh (silent - no cleanup job)
    + yourOccupancyBand : OccupancyBand
                                   ' V9 (D5): the CALLER's own live band -
                                   ' DETAIL read only; null for guests,
                                   ' anonymous callers and no-report users
    + yourOpenStatus : String      ' V22: the CALLER's own live open/closed state
                                   ' (DETAIL read only; same null rules as the band)
    + reviewStatus : ReviewStatus  ' V11 (community-review-queue v2): the community
                                   ' trust state; NEW rows are PUBLIC (amber "Newly
                                   ' added" treatment + unverified warning on detail)
    + reviewNote : String          ' V11: the admin's REJECT reason - /mine + admin rows
                                   ' only; null on the public projection
    + locationKind : LocationKind  ' V11: the private-home declaration (badge only -
                                   ' never hidden or demoted)
    + provenance : Provenance      ' V12 (shelter-provenance-taxonomy): the
                                   ' server-derived source answer; the UI never
                                   ' re-derives it
    + reportCount : int            ' entry-verification-meta: the TOTAL community
                                   ' report count (all types)
    + lastVerifiedAt : Instant     ' entry-verification-meta: the per-entry
                                   ' verification stamp; null = never verified
    + inaccurate : boolean         ' M10 slice 4 (V20 stamp): the moderator's
                                   ' "inaccurate" flag; the row stays visible
    + infoRequest : InfoRequest    ' M10 slice 3: the moderator-to-submitter
                                   ' exchange - /mine projection ONLY
    ' Lean projection: the full registry record (county, municipality,
    ' data-as-of, attribution) is stored in the DB but not dumped here -
    ' the UI gets only what the map needs. All V9 derivations are computed
    ' server-side in the batched projection - never client-computed.
    ' description/capacity: USER-submission details (stored since V3;
    ' null for registry rows).
  }

  class Occupancy <<record>> {
    ' Nested inside ShelterDto (V9, D4): the fresh (<= 2 h) occupancy block;
    ' null on the DTO when nothing is fresh (silent - no cleanup job).
    + band : OccupancyBand      ' the latest fresh band (ties: user id)
    + reportCount : int         ' fresh reports agreeing with it:
                                ' 1 = hedged copy, 2+ = firm
    + lastReportedAt : Instant  ' the newest fresh report's time
  }

  class OpenStatus <<record>> {
    ' Nested inside ShelterDto (V22, open-status): the fresh (<= 2 h)
    ' open/closed block; null on the DTO when nothing is fresh.
    + state : String            ' the latest fresh tap (OPEN / CLOSED)
    + reportedAt : Instant      ' the newest fresh tap's time
    + reportCount : int         ' fresh taps agreeing with it: 1 = hedged,
                                ' 2+ = firm
  }

  class InfoRequest <<record>> {
    ' Nested in ShelterDto + AdminShelterDto (M10 slice 3): the
    ' moderator-to-submitter exchange; /mine projection only (null on the
    ' public list and detail reads - the exchange is private).
    + message : String
    + requestedAt : Instant
    + replyMessage : String     ' null until the submitter answers (one-time)
    + repliedAt : Instant       ' null until answered
  }

  class ShelterReportRequest <<record>> {
    + type : ShelterReportType    ' @NotNull
    + detail : String             ' @Size(max = 500) - M11: stored for CLOSED / WRONG_LOCATION / OTHER (binary types drop it)
  }

  class OccupancyReportRequest <<record>> {
    + band : OccupancyBand        ' @NotNull
  }

  class CreateShelterRequest <<record>> {
    + name : String
    + latitude : double
    + longitude : double
    + description : String
    + capacity : Integer
    + locationKind : LocationKind  ' V11 (optional; default PUBLIC) - the private-home
                                   ' declaration checkbox; the created row is always
                                   ' review_status = NEW server-side
  }

  class UpdateShelterRequest <<record>> {
    ' M8: constraints IDENTICAL to CreateShelterRequest (create/update cannot drift);
    ' only these five fields are writable on an existing shelter
    + name : String
    + latitude : double
    + longitude : double
    + description : String
    + capacity : Integer
  }

  class ErrorResponse <<record>> {
    + timestamp : Instant
    + status : int
    + error : String
    + message : String
    + path : String
  }

  enum ShelterSourceFilter {
    REGISTRY
    USER
    ALL
  }

  ' V9 (shelter-trust-and-reports): the closed sets of the trust layer.
  enum ShelterReportType {
    NON_EXISTENT
    CLOSED
    OPEN_CONFIRMED
    WRONG_LOCATION
    OTHER
  }

  enum OccupancyBand {
    SPACE
    GETTING_FULL
    FULL
  }

  ' V11 (community-review-queue v2): the community trust lifecycle.
  enum ReviewStatus {
    NEW         ' just added (public immediately, amber "Newly added")
    CONFIRMED   ' community-checked (AUTO_CONFIRM promotion or admin CONFIRM)
    REJECTED    ' admin REJECT (hides via status = INACTIVE; restore -> NEW)
  }

  enum ReviewDecision {
    CONFIRM     ' admin manual promotion (the rare fallback)
    REJECT      ' admin hide + reason (reason required)
  }

  enum LocationKind {
    PUBLIC      ' the default
    PRIVATE     ' submitter-declared private home/shelter (badge only, never hidden)
  }
}

' ============ LOCATION RESOLUTION (shelter-location-input, 8686b99) ============
' app/ classes shown as contracts - defined in 01 (app context).
package "app - location resolution (contracts only)" {
  class LocationResolveService {
    + {static} WHITELISTED_HOST = "maps.app.goo.gl"
    + resolve(url : String) : Outcome   ' Resolved / NotFound / UpstreamFailure
  }

  note bottom of LocationResolveService
    Deliberately narrow (shelter-location-input): host whitelist
    (maps.app.goo.gl is the only host the client sends) + a manual
    <=3-hop redirect walk (every hop re-validated - auto-follow stays
    OFF) under a 10 s budget (3 s connect / 5 s read per hop).
    One generic 400 for every not-found variant (invalid input /
    non-whitelisted host / no extractable pair / outside Estonia -
    no enumeration); one generic 502 for every upstream failure
    (timeout / network / upstream 5xx - no upstream detail).
  end note

  interface RedirectClient {
    + fetch(url : String) : RedirectHop   ' one hop, status + Location header
    ' The seam that keeps LocationResolveService unit-testable.
  }

  class HttpUrlRedirectClient {
  }

  note bottom of HttpUrlRedirectClient
    Real hop fetcher: 3 s connect / 5 s read per hop, redirects NOT
    auto-followed, no cookies, fixed User-Agent; the status line +
    Location header only - never the body.
  end note

  class MapsUrlCoordinates {
    + {static} extract(url : String) : GeoPoint
  }

  note bottom of MapsUrlCoordinates
    The shared long-form map-URL pattern list, with the Estonia-bbox
    gate + (lng,lat) auto-swap - the same rules the frontend parser
    uses; both sides tested against the same fixture table.
  end note
}

' ============ TRUST LAYER (shelter-trust-and-reports, V9) ============
' app/ seams shown as contracts - defined in 01 (app context). The V9 tables:
' shelter_reports (UNIQUE shelter_id, user_id, type), shelter_occupancy_reports
' (UNIQUE shelter_id, user_id), report_actions (the durable throttle log),
' shelters.auto_hide_disarmed. Every report FK is ON DELETE CASCADE to
' shelters/users (a deleted shelter/user drops its reports with it).
' V11 (community-review-queue v2) adds: shelters.review_status (CHECK NEW/
' CONFIRMED/REJECTED, NOT NULL DEFAULT 'NEW'; USER rows backfilled NEW, registry
' rows CONFIRMED), shelters.review_note (the REJECT reason), shelters.location_kind
' (CHECK PUBLIC/PRIVATE, the private-home declaration) and moderation_actions
' (the append-only audit trail - shelter_id deliberately has NO FK: a delete
' records its row in the same transaction, the id dangles, the read-time join
' renders "Deleted shelter").
package "app - trust layer (contracts only)" {
  class ShelterReportService {
    + reportShelter(user : User, shelterId : long, type : ShelterReportType, detail : String) : void
    + reportOccupancy(user : User, shelterId : long, band : OccupancyBand) : void
    ' Verified-only (403, the submission vocabulary), 404 unknown shelter,
    ' 409 duplicate (shelter, user, type) BEFORE any throttle budget is
    ' consumed, 429 report throttle (10 report-type actions / rolling hour).
    ' The 4 -> 5 NON_EXISTENT insert auto-hides an ACTIVE shelter whose
    ' autoHideDisarmed is false - the ONLY auto-hide path (D1); later
    ' reports never re-hide (manual restore sets the flag).
    ' Occupancy: upsert - one live band per user per shelter, latest wins,
    ' updated_at refreshed. Display-only: never hides, recolors or filters.
  }

  interface ReportActionLog {
    + record(userId : long, action : Action) : void
    ' Action = SHELTER_REPORT | OCCUPANCY - one row per
    ' report-type action (any target, any type; occupancy re-PUTs count -
    ' a re-PUT updates one row and would be uncountable from the report
    ' tables). Counted over the trailing hour; at the cap (default 10,
    ' ReportProperties.maxActionsPerHour, 0 disables) reject WITHOUT
    ' recording (429 "Too many report requests"). The check-and-record is
    ' ATOMIC per user: persistence.JpaReportActionLog serializes it with a
    ' transaction-scoped Postgres advisory lock (pg_advisory_xact_lock,
    ' released on commit - the exact critical section).
  }

  interface ModerationAuditLog {
    ' V11 (community-review-queue v2 D4): the append-only moderation trail.
    + record(shelterId : long, actorId : long, action : Action, reason : String,
             previousStatus : ReviewStatus, newStatus : ReviewStatus) : void
    ' Action = STATUS_CHANGE | DELETE | REPORT_DISMISS | CONFIRM |
    ' AUTO_CONFIRM | REJECT. ONE row per
    ' moderation-relevant action, written in the SAME transaction as the
    ' action it records (no separate call, no async). Table: moderation_actions
    ' (V11); shelter_id has deliberately NO FK - a delete records its row in
    ' the same transaction, so the id dangles after the delete and the
    ' read-time name join renders "Deleted shelter". Actor = the acting user
    ' (the reporting user for AUTO_CONFIRM). Impls: JpaModerationAuditLog
    ' (persistence) + the in-memory test double.
  }

  interface ShelterReportRepository {
    + countByTypeForShelterIds(ids : Collection<Long>) : List<ReportTypeCount>
    ' one report per (shelter, user, type) - the per-target unique bound
  }

  interface ShelterOccupancyRepository {
    + findFreshByShelterIds(ids : Collection<Long>, freshSince : Instant) : List<ShelterOccupancyReport>
    ' the 2 h freshness window is applied in SQL; the derivation
    ' (latest band wins, agreeing count, newest timestamp) is in memory
  }

}

' ============ CONTRACT WITH OTHER CONTEXTS (interfaces only) ============
ShelterController --> ShelterQueryService : GET + GET /mine
ShelterController --> ShelterService : POST / PUT / DELETE (app/01)
ShelterController --> CreateShelterRequest : parses body
ShelterController --> UpdateShelterRequest : parses PUT body
ShelterController --> ErrorResponse : 400/401/403/404/429
ShelterQueryService --> ShelterRepository : reads (interface, 01)
ShelterQueryService --> UserRepository : creator verification batch (interface, 01)
ShelterQueryService --> Shelter : maps to DTO
ShelterQueryService --> ShelterDto : returns

' ---- trust layer (V9, shelter-trust-and-reports) ----
ShelterController --> ShelterReportService : reports + occupancy (app/V9)
ShelterController --> ShelterReportRequest : parses report body
ShelterController --> OccupancyReportRequest : parses occupancy body
ShelterReportService --> ShelterReportRepository : interface (V9)
ShelterReportService --> ShelterOccupancyRepository : interface (V9)
ShelterReportService ..> ReportActionLog : check-and-record (429 at the cap)
ShelterReportService ..> Shelter : the ONLY auto-hide path (4 -> 5 NON_EXISTENT)
ShelterQueryService --> ShelterReportRepository : report counts by type (one batched query)
ShelterQueryService --> ShelterOccupancyRepository : fresh occupancy rows (one batched query)
' ---- admin moderation (admin-moderation D3/D4) ----
AdminController --> AdminModerationService : all /admin/* writes + queues
AdminController ..> UserRepository : fresh isAdmin(userId) kind lookup PER REQUEST (D2)
AdminController ..> ErrorResponse : 401 anonymous (entry point) / 403 non-admin
AdminModerationService --> ShelterQueryService : findAllForAdmin (the same batched projection - no N+1)
AdminModerationService ..> Shelter : the ONLY manual status path + the ONLY admin delete (USER rows)
AdminModerationService ..> ShelterReport : dismiss stamps dismissed_at (once, idempotent; the row is kept)
AdminModerationService ..> ModerationAuditLog : V11 - one audit row per action, SAME transaction (append-only)
AdminModerationService ..> ErrorResponse : 404 unknown id / 409 import-owned registry row (D4)

' ---- location resolution (POST /api/geo/resolve) ----
LocationController --> LocationResolveService : resolve(url)
LocationController --> LocationResolveRequest : parses body
LocationController --> LocationResolvedDto : returns
LocationController ..> RateLimiter : per-IP 5/min bucket (geoResolveRateLimiter, auth/03)
LocationController ..> ErrorResponse : 400 / 429 / 502
LocationResolveService ..> RedirectClient : hop walk (seam)
HttpUrlRedirectClient ..|> RedirectClient : real hop fetcher
LocationResolveService --> MapsUrlCoordinates : pair extraction on the final URL

ShelterSourceFilter ..> ShelterRepository : ?source= maps to findAllActiveBySourceIn()
ShelterSourceFilter --> ShelterSource : REGISTRY={PAASETEAMET,MUNICIPALITY}, USER={USER}, ALL={all}

note bottom of AdminController
  ADMIN MODERATION (admin-moderation) - the trust layer's human lever.
  Authorization (D2): FRESH kind lookup per request - the JWT's userId is
  loaded and UserKind.ADMIN is required (no role claim in the token, so a
  demotion takes effect on the next request). 401 anonymous (the security
  entry point - /admin/** is in the authenticated set) -> 403 authenticated
  non-admin -> 404 unknown id -> 409 registry row under a write (D4) ->
  400 malformed body. All writes are 204, single-row, no bulk endpoints
  (exception: the review decision answers 200 {"ok": true}).

  GET  /admin/shelters?status=&source=&q=      every shelter incl. hidden,
       id-ordered, batched trust fields + the submitter's name; status/
       source exact-match, q = case-insensitive name/address substring
  POST /admin/shelters/{id}/status             manual hide/restore (USER rows
       only; registry -> 409 import-owned). A RESTORE sets autoHideDisarmed
       = true - permanently disarms auto-hide (V9 D1: later NON_EXISTENT
       reports never re-hide)
  DELETE /admin/shelters/{id}                   hard delete (cascade: shelter
       reports, occupancy, open-status - all FKs ON DELETE CASCADE); USER
       rows only; the only path that deletes a USER row for the trust layer
  GET  /admin/reports?shelterId=               shelter-report queue, newest
       first, with the shelter's LIVE status + the reporter's profile name
       + email (admin-only data - never exposed outside /admin/*)
  POST /admin/reports/{id}/dismiss             mark resolved - stamps
       dismissed_at ONCE (idempotent); the row is KEPT (records the
       resolution, never deletes)
  POST /admin/shelters/{id}/review             V11 (community-review-queue v2):
       {"action": CONFIRM | REJECT, "reason"?} - CONFIRM sets review_status =
       CONFIRMED (note cleared, status untouched); REJECT requires a reason and
       sets review_status = REJECTED + status = INACTIVE (the existing hide).
       USER rows only; 400 blank reason on REJECT
  GET  /admin/audit?limit=                     V11: the append-only moderation
       trail, newest first (limit 1..200, default 100); deleted shelters render
       "Deleted shelter" (shelter_id FK-free by design)

  D4: registry rows (source != USER) are READ-ONLY for admins - the
  registry import owns their lifecycle and rebuilds them as ACTIVE on every
  run, so an admin edit would silently revert (the UI offers no actions for
  them; the lever for bad registry data is upstream, Päästeamet).
end note

note bottom of ShelterController
  GET  /api/shelters?source=REGISTRY|USER|ALL  (public - VIEW_MAP baseline;
       ACTIVE rows ONLY since V9 - auto-hidden shelters are absent; the optional
       trust filter hasCapacity composes with source, applied in the
       projection. M11: the rating filter is gone - a stray param is
       ignored, not an error)
  GET  /api/shelters/{id}                      (public - ALL statuses, incl.
       auto-hidden; the detail read additionally carries yourOccupancyBand)
  POST /api/shelters                           (Bearer JWT, canWrite() check;
       409 when the caller already has 10 ACTIVE USER shelters - ADMIN kind
       exempt; deletions and auto-hidden rows free the cap)
  GET  /api/shelters/mine                      (Bearer JWT - the CALLER's shelters,
       ALL statuses incl. auto-hidden, NOT public)
  PUT    /api/shelters/{id}                    (Bearer JWT, author-only USER rows)
  DELETE /api/shelters/{id}                    (Bearer JWT, author-only; reports + occupancy cascade)
  POST /api/shelters/{id}/reports              (Bearer JWT + verified -> 200 {damped};
       404 unknown shelter; 409 duplicate (shelter, user, type) - checked before
       the throttle budget; 429 report throttle. The 5th NON_EXISTENT auto-hides.
       M11: detail (<= 500) stored for CLOSED / WRONG_LOCATION / OTHER, ignored
       for the binary types; the admin queue surfaces it.
       Verified-only: 403 "Reporting requires a verified account")
  PUT  /api/shelters/{id}/occupancy            (Bearer JWT + verified -> 204 upsert;
       one live band per user per shelter, latest wins; 404 unknown; 429 throttle;
       no 409 - a re-send is the update. Display-only, fresh <= 2 h at read time)
  POST /api/geo/resolve                        (Bearer JWT, per-IP 5/min -> 429;
       LocationController - 400 ONE generic message when no pair / outside
       Estonia / non-whitelisted host; 502 ONE generic retry-later message on
       upstream failure - no enumeration, no upstream detail)
  Author check (PUT/DELETE): 404 if absent, 403 if not the author - registry rows and
  legacy created_by-NULL rows are unmanageable by anyone (ids are public, so
  403-vs-404 leaks nothing). PUT re-checks the Estonia bbox - one shared gate with
  POST, so create/update cannot drift.
  Deferred: nearest/bbox queries need GeoService + PostGIS GIST index.
  Paging deferred: Estonia-scale data is small; add limit/offset when it grows.
end note

note right of ShelterQueryService
  shelters.created_by (V7): BIGINT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL +
  idx_shelters_created_by. addPlace sets it (the submitting user); NULL for registry
  rows and pre-V7 legacy USER rows. GET /mine queries it; PUT/DELETE gate on it.
end note

@enduml

@startuml
title Shelter Map - API Flows (sequence)
actor Client

participant "ShelterController" as SC
participant "ShelterQueryService" as SQS
participant "ShelterRepository" as REPO
participant "ShelterService" as SS
participant "ShelterReportService" as SRS
participant "ReportActionLog" as RAL
participant "AdminController" as ADC
participant "AdminModerationService" as AMS
participant "LocationController" as LC
participant "LocationResolveService" as LRS
participant "HttpUrlRedirectClient" as HRC
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== 1. GET /api/shelters?source=USER (public, ACTIVE rows only) ==
Client -> SC : GET /api/shelters?source=USER
note right of SC
  V9: the public list is status = ACTIVE ONLY (auto-hidden shelters
  are absent). The optional trust filter hasCapacity composes with
  source (M11: the rating filter is gone - a stray param is ignored,
  not an error).
end note
SC -> SQS : findAll(USER, hasCapacity?, provenance?)
SQS -> REPO : findAllActiveBySourceIn([USER])
REPO -> DB : SELECT ... WHERE source IN (...) AND status = 'ACTIVE'
REPO --> SQS : List<Shelter>
SQS -> DB : report counts by type + fresh occupancy (one batched pass - no N+1)
SQS --> SC : List<ShelterDto> (with nonexistentReports, openStatus, occupancy)
SC --> Client : 200 [ShelterDto]

== 2. POST /api/shelters (Bearer JWT, verified user) ==
Client -> SC : POST /api/shelters {name, lat, lng, ...}
SC -> SS : addPlace(user, shelter)
SS -> DB : save shelter (status = ACTIVE, source = USER, created_by = user)
SS --> SC : Shelter
SC --> Client : 201 + Location

== 5. GET /api/shelters/mine (Bearer JWT) ==
Client -> SC : GET /api/shelters/mine
SC -> SQS : findByCreatedBy(me)
SQS -> REPO : findByCreatedBy(userId)
REPO -> DB : SELECT ... WHERE created_by = ?
REPO --> SQS : List<Shelter>
SQS --> SC : List<ShelterDto> (never other users' or registry rows)
SC --> Client : 200 [ShelterDto]

== 6. PUT /api/shelters/{id} (Bearer JWT, author-only) ==
Client -> SC : PUT {name, lat, lng, description, capacity}
SC -> REPO : findById(id)
alt absent
  SC --> Client : 404 (uniform ErrorResponse)
else not the author (or a registry / legacy created_by-NULL row)
  SC --> Client : 403
else author
  note right of SC: bbox re-check (shared gate with POST) -> 400 outside Estonia
  SC -> SS : updatePlace(updated)  ' the five fields only
  SS -> DB : UPDATE (status/source/createdBy/created_at untouched)
  SC --> Client : 200 ShelterDto
end

== 7. DELETE /api/shelters/{id} (Bearer JWT, author-only) ==
Client -> SC : DELETE
SC -> REPO : findById(id) + author check (404 / 403 as above)
SC -> DB : DELETE shelter (reports + occupancy cascade via the DB)
SC --> Client : 204 No Content

== 9. POST /api/geo/resolve (Bearer JWT, per-IP 5/min) ==
Client -> LC : POST /api/geo/resolve {url}
alt per-IP bucket empty (5/min)
  LC --> Client : 429 (uniform ErrorResponse)
else
  LC -> LRS : resolve(url)   ' host whitelist: maps.app.goo.gl only
  LRS -> HRC : fetch(url)  (one hop, NO auto-follow; 3 s connect / 5 s read, 10 s budget)
  alt 3xx with Location (re-validated hop, <= 3 total)
    HRC --> LRS : RedirectHop(3xx, Location) - walk continues
  else terminal response
    HRC --> LRS : RedirectHop(status, Location?)
  end
  alt pair extracted on the final URL (bbox gate + auto-swap)
    LRS --> LC : Outcome.Resolved(latitude, longitude)
    LC --> Client : 200 {latitude, longitude}
  else invalid input / other host / no pair / outside Estonia
    LRS --> LC : Outcome.NotFound
    LC --> Client : 400 ONE generic message (no enumeration)
  else timeout / network failure / upstream 5xx
    LRS --> LC : Outcome.UpstreamFailure
    LC --> Client : 502 ONE generic retry-later message (no upstream detail)
  end
end

== 10. POST /api/shelters/{id}/reports (Bearer JWT, verified user) ==
Client -> SC : POST /api/shelters/{id}/reports {type, detail?}
SC -> SRS : reportShelter(user, id, type, detail)
alt no/invalid token (guests cannot report)
  SC --> Client : 401 (uniform ErrorResponse)
else registered but NOT verified
  SRS --> Client : 403 "Reporting requires a verified account"
else unknown shelter
  SRS --> Client : 404
else duplicate (shelter, user, type)
  SRS --> Client : 409 "This report has already been submitted" (no throttle budget consumed)
else report throttle (10 report-type actions / rolling hour)
  SRS -> RAL : record(user, SHELTER_REPORT)
  RAL --> SRS : at cap -> reject WITHOUT recording
  SRS --> Client : 429 "Too many report requests"
else
  SRS -> RAL : record(user, SHELTER_REPORT)  (advisory-locked check-and-record)
  SRS -> DB : INSERT shelter_reports (UNIQUE shelter_id, user_id, type)
  alt type = NON_EXISTENT and the count goes 4 -> 5 (shelter ACTIVE, not disarmed)
    SRS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET status = INACTIVE (auto-hide, exactly-once trigger)
  end
  alt type = OPEN_CONFIRMED and the USER row is still review_status = NEW and reporter != submitter (V11)
    SRS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET review_status = 'CONFIRMED' (same transaction)
    SRS -> DB : INSERT moderation_actions (AUTO_CONFIRM, actor = the reporting user)
  end
  SRS --> Client : 200 {"damped": true|false}
end
note over SRS
  The auto-hide is the ONLY auto-hide path. After a manual status change
  (admin restore sets auto_hide_disarmed = true) later reports increment
  the count but never re-hide. CLOSED / OPEN_CONFIRMED feed the fresh
  open/closed display block only (V22: the latest fresh tap wins, 1 fresh
  tap = hedged, 2+ = firm) - they never hide.
  V11: OPEN_CONFIRMED additionally carries the NEW -> CONFIRMED promotion
  (community-review-queue v2 D2) - in the SAME transaction, audited
  AUTO_CONFIRM; the submitter's own positive report never promotes.
end note

== 12. PUT /api/shelters/{id}/occupancy (Bearer JWT, verified user) ==
Client -> SRS : PUT /api/shelters/{id}/occupancy {band}
alt NOT verified
  SRS --> Client : 403
else unknown shelter
  SRS --> Client : 404
else report throttle (re-PUTs count against the budget)
  SRS --> Client : 429
else
  SRS -> RAL : record(user, OCCUPANCY)
  SRS -> DB : UPSERT shelter_occupancy_reports (shelter_id, user_id) - latest band wins, updated_at refreshed
  SRS --> Client : 204 No Content
end
note over SRS, DB
  Occupancy is DISPLAY-ONLY: it never hides, recolors or filters. The read-time
  derivation (GET /api/shelters*): fresh = updated_at within the last 2 h (checked
  in SQL, no cleanup job); the most recent fresh band wins; reportCount = fresh
  reports agreeing with it (1 = "Reported full" hedged, 2+ = "Full" firm);
  nothing fresh -> no occupancy shown.
end note

== 13. Admin moderation (Bearer JWT + ADMIN kind - fresh lookup per request) ==
Client -> ADC : any /admin/* call
ADC -> DB : load the JWT's userId, check kind = ADMIN (fresh lookup, D2 - no JWT claim)
alt anonymous (no/invalid token)
  ADC --> Client : 401 (the security entry point - /admin/** is in the authenticated set)
else authenticated but NOT admin-kind
  ADC --> Client : 403 "Admin access required" (AdminAccessException - a demotion takes effect on this very request)
end

== 13a. GET /admin/shelters?status=&source=&q= ==
ADC -> AMS : listShelters(status, source, q)
AMS -> DB : every shelter (ALL statuses incl. hidden) + the same batched trust pass as the public list (no N+1)
AMS --> ADC : List<AdminShelterDto> (+ the submitter's profile name)
ADC --> Client : 200 [AdminShelterDto]

== 13b. POST /admin/shelters/{id}/status {status: ACTIVE|INACTIVE} ==
ADC -> AMS : setShelterStatus(id, target)
AMS -> DB : findById(id)
alt absent
  ADC --> Client : 404
else source != USER (a registry row - import-owned, D4)
  ADC --> Client : 409 "Registry shelters are import-owned and cannot be moderated here"
else restore (INACTIVE -> ACTIVE)
  AMS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET auto_hide_disarmed = true, status = 'ACTIVE'  ' the disarm is permanent (V9 D1)
  alt the row's review_status = REJECTED (V11)
    AMS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET review_status = 'NEW'  ' it starts over - a rejected row does not come back as CONFIRMED
  end
  AMS -> DB : INSERT moderation_actions (STATUS_CHANGE, previous/new review_status)
  ADC --> Client : 204 No Content
else hide (ACTIVE -> INACTIVE)
  AMS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET status = 'INACTIVE'
  AMS -> DB : INSERT moderation_actions (STATUS_CHANGE, previous/new review_status)
  ADC --> Client : 204 No Content
end

== 13c. DELETE /admin/shelters/{id} (USER rows only) ==
ADC -> AMS : deleteShelter(id)
AMS -> DB : DELETE shelter (USER rows only - registry 409, absent 404; ON DELETE CASCADE -> shelter reports, occupancy, open-status)
ADC --> Client : 204 No Content

== 13d. POST /admin/reports/{id}/dismiss ==
ADC -> AMS : dismissReport(id)
alt absent
  ADC --> Client : 404
else not yet dismissed
  AMS -> DB : UPDATE shelter_reports SET dismissed_at = now()  (stamped ONCE - a re-dismiss is a no-op; the row is KEPT)
  ADC --> Client : 204 No Content
end

note over ADC, AMS
  Queue: GET /admin/reports?shelterId= (newest first; the shelter's LIVE status +
  the reporter's profile name/email - admin-only data, never exposed outside
  /admin/*). Reporter identity is served from this API ONLY.
  V11: EVERY action above (status change, delete, dismiss) writes its
  moderation_actions audit row in the SAME transaction - see 13f/13g.
end note

== 13f. POST /admin/shelters/{id}/review {action: CONFIRM|REJECT, reason?} (V11) ==
ADC -> AMS : reviewShelter(moderatorId, id, action, reason)
AMS -> DB : findById(id)
alt absent
  ADC --> Client : 404
else source != USER (a registry row - import-owned, D4)
  ADC --> Client : 409 "Registry shelters are import-owned and cannot be moderated here"
else action = REJECT and reason missing/blank
  ADC --> Client : 400 (standard vocabulary - the reason is REQUIRED to reject)
else action = CONFIRM
  AMS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET review_status = 'CONFIRMED', review_note = NULL  (status untouched - CONFIRM does not un-hide)
  AMS -> DB : INSERT moderation_actions (CONFIRM, previous -> CONFIRMED)
else action = REJECT
  AMS -> DB : UPDATE shelters SET review_status = 'REJECTED', review_note = ?, status = 'INACTIVE'  (the existing hide mechanism)
  AMS -> DB : INSERT moderation_actions (REJECT, reason, previous -> REJECTED)
end
AMS --> ADC : done (single-row transaction, audit row included)
ADC --> Client : 200 {"ok": true}
note over AMS
  The rare manual fallback (community-review-queue v2 D2) - the PRIMARY promotion
  path is automatic (the AUTO_CONFIRM in flow 10). A CONFIRM of an INACTIVE row
  does NOT un-hide it - visibility is the status endpoint's job (13b).
end note

== 13g. GET /admin/audit?limit= (V11) ==
ADC -> AMS : listAudit(moderatorId, limit)  ' default 100; 1..200 else 400
AMS -> DB : SELECT ... FROM moderation_actions ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC LIMIT ?
AMS -> DB : batched read-time joins: shelter names + moderator names (one lookup each - no N+1)
AMS --> ADC : List<AdminAuditDto>  ' a deleted shelter renders "Deleted shelter" (shelter_id is FK-free by design)
ADC --> Client : 200 [AdminAuditDto]
@enduml
